    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Protocol 03</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Use a handheld light source to examine hidden seams.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #a855f722; color: #a855f7; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">04</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Protocol 04</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Record any new findings in the handover form.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #ec489922; color: #ec4899; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">05</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Protocol 05</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Photograph the issue for the carrier’s claim file.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<p>The second stage involves odometer verification. The vehicle’s odometer reading is read carefully, noting the exact number of kilometers or miles. This reading is then matched against the mileage recorded on the LR bilty (Logistics Receipt Bilty).</p>
<p>Any variance greater than the allowable tolerance (typically ±5 km) triggers an immediate audit. The driver prints the LR bilty, marks the verified mileage, and signs it. The recipient also signs to confirm the reading, creating a dual‑signature record that protects both the carrier and the customer from mileage disputes.</p>

<ul>
<li>Read the odometer with a calibrated meter.</li>
<li>Cross‑check with the LR bilty mileage field.</li>
<li>Mark the verified reading on the bilty.</li>
<li>Both parties sign the bilty.</li>
<li>Attach the signed bilty to the delivery docket.</li>
</ul>

<p>The final stage is the signed condition sign‑off. After the visual inspection and odometer check are complete, the recipient signs a condition sheet that confirms the vehicle’s state and the mileage.</p>
<p>This signed sheet is scanned into the carrier’s system and emailed to the logistics manager for audit purposes. Once all documents are signed and uploaded, the handover is officially closed, and the delivery is logged as successful.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>



